.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/5713/movie.293x165.jpg?t=1447353186","hls":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/40800/3587/48c3f6f70f8d244dd58c9a7d365c3796ed0dfc0b/1750485478/hls_264_master.m3u8?t=1447353186","mp4":"https://cdn.akamai.steamstatic.com/steam/apps/5713/movie480.mp4"}],"genres":["Indie"],"features":["Single-player","Steam Achievements","Remote Play on TV","Steam Trading Cards","Family Sharing"],"platforms":{"windows":true,"mac":true,"linux":true},"controller":"full","dev":["Team Meat"],"pub":[],"released":"Nov 30, 2010","meta":87,"langs":["English","Russian"],"min":[["OS","Microsoft\u00ae Windows\u00ae XP / Vista / 7 (Windows 8 is not officially supported)"],["Processor","1.4GHz or faster"],["Memory","1 GB RAM"],["Graphics","Graphics Card made within the last 4 years (Pixel Shader 3.0, Vertex Shader 3.0)"],["DirectX\u00ae","DirectX\u00ae 9.0c"],["Hard Drive","300 MB"],["Controller Support","Microsoft Xbox 360 Controller or Direct Input compatible controller"]],"rec":[],"deck":3,"blurb":"Rescuing a girlfriend made of bandages is the goal for a cube of meat, who must get past a tuxedo-clad fetus in a jar. Super Meat Boy sends him wall-jumping across buzz saws, crumbling caves and worlds that include hospitals, factories and hell in a punishing precision platformer.\n\nThe difficulty takes cues from NES classics such as Mega Man 2 and the Japanese Super Mario Bros. 2, starting hard and climbing to brutal. There are more than 300 levels, and the Steam version adds a playable character called Head Crab. Controls are tight and retries are instant, so it suits players who enjoy fast, twitchy platforming and can take repeated failure."}}